## Context

PR #1009 (ticket 0551) added `src/aedist/matching/lp.py` as a prerequisite of
the phase-collision rule in `experiments/render.mk`, because the analysis
script imports it. Review found sibling targets with the same gap: any rule
whose script reaches the matcher through `reconcile.py` (recognition
matrices, source concordance, wiki recall bar, ...) lists `reconcile.py` but
not `matching/lp.py` / `matching/phased.py`, so a matcher change does not
mark those artifacts stale. The 0551 session had to invoke the rebuilds
manually.

## Relevant files

- `experiments/render.mk` — prerequisite lists
- `src/aedist/reconcile.py`, `src/aedist/matching/*.py` — actual import graph
- `tickets/closed/0530-*.erg`, `tickets/0535-*.erg` — prior prerequisite work

## Actions

1. Trace which render.mk rules run scripts that (transitively) import
   `aedist.matching.*`.
2. Add the missing prerequisites — or a shared `MATCHER_SRCS` variable.
3. Consider extending the 0535 standing adherence test to catch transitive
   import-vs-prereq drift for the matching package.

## Test

- Red first: a test (or `make -n` probe) showing that touching
  `src/aedist/matching/lp.py` does not invalidate
  `report/inputs/generated/macros_exp2_matrix_naive.tex`.

## Exit criteria

- [ ] Every render.mk rule whose script imports the matcher lists the
      matching sources as prerequisites
- [ ] `make check` green
